        You will be given the root cause of a bug, the commit message and the corresponding patch.
        You need to extract all code statements that lead to the bug from the patch, based on the root cause and the commit message.

        Root cause:
        The root cause of the bug was the incorrect management of the parameter count in the `sampgdk_callback_invoke` function, where it relied on `amx->paramcount` instead of receiving the actual parameter count as an argument. This led to potential stack popping errors when callbacks were invoked, particularly when the callback itself called `amx_Exec()`. As a result, arguments could be incorrectly treated, causing inconsistent behavior or crashes.

        Commit message:
        Fix bad params in OnPublicCall()

This fixes a bug introduced in commit 0dc90c645e0d73d1c92a51e8efd20021ac399a10.  

        Patch:

 static int AMXAPI _sampgdk_amxhooks_Exec(AMX *amx, cell *retval, int index) {
   bool proceed = true;
   int error = AMX_ERR_NONE;
   int paramcount = amx->paramcount;

   /* We have to reset amx->paramcount at this point so that if the callback
-   * itself calls amx_Exec() it won't pop out arguments off the stack.
+   * itself calls amx_Exec() it won't pop our arguments off the stack.
    */
   amx->paramcount = 0;

   /* Since filterscripts don't use main() we can assume that the AMX
    * that executes main() is indeed the main AMX i.e. the gamemode.
    */
   if (index == AMX_EXEC_MAIN) {
     /* This extra check is needed in order to stop OnGameModeInit()
      * from being called twice in a row after a gmx.
      */
     if (_sampgdk_amxhooks_main_amx != amx && amx != NULL) {
-      sampgdk_callback_invoke(amx, "OnGameModeInit", retval);
+      sampgdk_callback_invoke(amx, "OnGameModeInit", paramcount, retval);
       _sampgdk_amxhooks_main_amx = amx;
     }
   } else {
     if (index != AMX_EXEC_CONT && (amx == _sampgdk_amxhooks_main_amx ||
                                    amx == sampgdk_fakeamx_amx())) {
       char name[_SAMPGDK_AMXHOOKS_MAX_PUBLIC_NAME];
       sampgdk_strcpy(name, _sampgdk_amxhooks_public_name, sizeof(name));
-      proceed = sampgdk_callback_invoke(amx, name, retval);
+      proceed = sampgdk_callback_invoke(amx, name, paramcount, retval);
     }
   }

   sampgdk_hook_remove(_sampgdk_amxhooks_Exec_hook);
   sampgdk_hook_install(_sampgdk_amxhooks_Callback_hook);

   if (proceed && index != AMX_EXEC_GDK) {
     amx->paramcount = paramcount;
     error = amx_Exec(amx, retval, index);
   } else {
     amx->paramcount = 0;
     amx->stk += paramcount * sizeof(cell);
   }

   sampgdk_hook_remove(_sampgdk_amxhooks_Callback_hook);
   sampgdk_hook_install(_sampgdk_amxhooks_Exec_hook);

   return error;
 }



